---
import ArticleLayout from '../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
import { getPost } from '../../data/posts';

const post = getPost('amazon-storefront');
---

<ArticleLayout
  kind="blog"
  post={post}
  title="Amazon Storefront Complete Guide"
  highlight="Complete Guide"
  metaTitle={`${post.title} | Share It Studio Blog`}
>
  <div class="article-body">
    <!-- Cabecera del Artículo -->
    <header class="post-header">
      <p class="intro">
        At this point, you surely have your products on Amazon and are likely a Brand Registered Seller looking to
        increase conversions. Maybe you've considered creating a dedicated website for your brand but don't know where
        to start.
      </p>
      <p>
        Amazon has the perfect answer for you: <strong>Amazon Storefront</strong>! It is one of the most effective ways
        to generate brand awareness and make your product listings stand out from the crowd.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Sección 1: ¿Qué es? -->
    <section id="what-is-amazon-storefront">
      <h2>What Is Amazon Storefront (Stores)?</h2>
      <p>
        Amazon Stores (or Storefront) is a feature designed for sellers who are growing their businesses and want a
        dedicated destination to showcase their entire product catalog organized by custom categories.
      </p>
      <p>
        It acts as the ultimate landing page for advertisers, allowing you to communicate your brand story, explain what
        makes your products special, and highlight key benefits using captivating photos, custom graphics, and video
        content that elevates the overall shopping experience.
      </p>

      <h3>Key Advantages of Amazon Stores:</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Behavioral Insights:</strong> Access robust analytics to analyze shopping behavior, allowing you to
          refine your content, optimize ad campaigns, and drive repeat visits.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Centralized Campaign Management:</strong> Manage external and internal ad campaigns from a central
          brand hub.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Off-Amazon SEO:</strong> Custom storefronts can rank on Google Search results, boosting your organic
          SEO both on Google and Amazon.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <aside class="cta-callout">
        <p>
          Looking to elevate your Amazon Store design? <strong>Contact us today</strong> to build a high-converting
          storefront that sets your brand apart!
        </p>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <!-- Sección 2: Componentes / Tiles -->
    <section id="storefront-tiles">
      <h2>Understanding Amazon Storefront Tiles</h2>
      <p>
        Amazon Storefronts are built using <strong>tiles</strong>—modular building blocks that allow you to shape and
        customize your brand's landing page. Below are the core tile types available:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Header Tile:</strong> Appears at the top of your Store and includes a hero image, brand logo, and
          navigation menu bar.
          <ul>
            <li>
              <em>Safe Zone Requirement:</em> Amazon requires a central "safe zone" because up to 30% of the hero image
              may be cropped (15% from the left and right sides) depending on screen size. Keep critical visual elements
              within this central zone.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </li>

        <li>
          <strong>Image Tile:</strong> Links directly to a Store sub-page or a specific product detail page.
          <ul>
            <li>
              <em>Link Title Overlay:</em> Adding link titles covers part of the image (approx. 19% at the bottom for
              medium/full-width rectangular tiles, and approx. 12% for square tiles).
            </li>
          </ul>
        </li>

        <li>
          <strong>Shoppable Image Tile:</strong> Showcases up to 6 products with interactive hotspot points. Shoppers
          can click points to view essential product information (title, image, Prime badge, price, star rating) and
          proceed to purchase via the product detail page.
        </li>

        <li>
          <strong>Video Tile:</strong> Interactive video player complete with play/pause, volume, and full-screen
          controls. Requires both a video file and a custom cover image for its resting state. Plays inline on desktop
          and full-screen on mobile devices.
        </li>

        <li>
          <strong>Background Video Tile:</strong> Auto-plays and loops on silent whenever visible on screen. Designed to
          set a visual mood without player controls on both desktop and mobile layouts.
        </li>

        <li>
          <strong>Product Tile:</strong> Highlights a single product alongside pricing, Prime status, and direct detail
          page links.
          <ul>
            <li>
              <em>Medium Tiles:</em> Allow custom product titles and short descriptions.
            </li>
            <li>
              <em>Full-Width Product Details:</em> Automatically pulls live data from the detail page, including an "Add
              to Cart" call to action.
            </li>
            <li>
              <em>Full-Width Product Editorial:</em> Displays custom titles and editorial descriptions.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </li>

        <li>
          <strong>Algorithmic Tiles:</strong> Dynamic tiles that update automatically based on Amazon data:
          <ul>
            <li>
              <em>Best Seller Tile:</em> Displays up to 5 top-selling products associated with your registered brand.
            </li>
            <li>
              <em>Recommended Products Tile:</em> Shows up to 5 personalized product recommendations based on the
              shopper's individual browsing history.
            </li>
            <li>
              <em>Featured Deals Tile:</em> Automatically displays products with active promotional pricing for the
              duration of the promotion.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Sección 3: Por qué usarlo -->
    <section id="why-use-storefront">
      <h2>Why Should You Use Amazon Storefront?</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>100% Free:</strong> Amazon Storefront is available at no additional cost for Brand Registered sellers.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No Coding Required:</strong> Built with an intuitive drag-and-drop tile editor that requires zero HTML
          knowledge.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Customizable Brand URL:</strong> Get a short, professional web address (e.g.,{' '}
          <code>amazon.com/yourbrand</code>) ideal for off-site marketing.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Enhanced Brand Awareness:</strong> Express your brand identity using rich media assets to build
          long-lasting buyer connections.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Cross-Promotion &amp; Bundling:</strong> Group complementary product lines to encourage multi-item
          purchases and higher average order value (AOV).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Intuitive Category Organization:</strong> Organize vast catalogs into clear, navigable pages so
          shoppers can find products effortlessly.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Powerful Analytics:</strong> Access dedicated dashboard metrics including traffic sources, order
          volume, total units sold, lead tags, and mobile app traffic data.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Sección 4: Buenas Prácticas -->
    <section id="best-practices">
      <h2>Amazon Storefront Best Practices</h2>
      <ol class="best-practices-list">
        <li>
          <strong>Promote Your Custom URL:</strong> Utilize your custom Amazon URL across external marketing campaigns
          (social media, email, Google Ads) to drive targeted traffic.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Prioritize Visual Quality:</strong> Use high-resolution photography, professional graphics, and
          engaging videos to foster trust and brand loyalty.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Tailor Your Layout:</strong> Customize store templates to align closely with your brand identity
          rather than relying on default presets.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Separate Distinct Product Lines:</strong> Create dedicated sub-pages for unrelated product categories
          (e.g., keep sports gear separated from home cleaning products).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Maintain Familiar UI Elements:</strong> Position recognizable Amazon navigation icons and terminology
          clearly so buyers feel comfortable browsing.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Feature Top Performers First:</strong> Place unique selling propositions (USPs) and best-selling
          products near the top of the homepage for maximum immediate impact.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Leverage Shoppable Images:</strong> Use hotspot tags on lifestyle photos to shorten the customer
          journey from discovery to checkout.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Keep Navigation Clear:</strong> Ensure main category links are visible near the header so shoppers can
          immediately explore your full catalog.
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <!-- Sección 5: Conclusión y CTA -->
    <section id="conclusion">
      <h2>Conclusion</h2>
      <p>
        Implementing these Amazon Storefront strategies will help increase brand awareness, enhance organic visibility,
        and drive sustainable long-term sales. Pair your storefront with Amazon Posts to further accelerate your channel
        growth!
      </p>
      <p>
        <em>
          Need expert help setting up or optimizing your Amazon Storefront? Book a free marketing consultation with our
          team today!
        </em>
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</ArticleLayout>
